      statement: "For each taint source-to-sink path reported by the taint analyzer: (a) the path must be realizable — every edge corresponds to actual data flow, not just call reachability, and (b) sanitizers on the path must actually neutralize the taint category in question. Structural (call-graph-only) results must be explicitly labeled as approximate."  # dc3c
      root_cause: "ADR-0017 work not yet started. Structural taint flow (Phase 1) will have high false positive rate by design; DDG-backed flow (Phase 2+) will improve precision."  # dc3c
      fix: "Phased implementation: Phase 1 structural BFS with labels, Phase 2 CFG+DDG precision, Phase 3 function summaries, Phase 4 cross-language."  # dc3c
